abstract: >-
  FRACMATH is a MATLAB framework for finite element simulation of fracture in
  quasibrittle materials using scalar isotropic continuum damage mechanics,
  modified von Mises equivalent strain, exponential softening, and
  direction-dependent Oliver crack-band regularization.
  The current SoftwareX companions include ten material-point examples,
  completed exact-mesh fixed-increment bending comparisons, element-area
  versus Oliver width, and two equivalent-strain definitions verified on CPU.
  A hybrid GPU backend retains CPU sparse assembly and factorization.
  Three 3D pure-tension meshes provide a numerical mesh-consistency check;
  mixed-mode and torsion fields are qualitative demonstrations.
  Earlier hardware observations and partial UMAT profiles are optional
  archives. The v1.1.1 DOI identifies the numerical-core archive, not a new
  release of the current comparison companions.
